### Conflicting claims compared (2nd pass)

- Official docs: identity undisclosed, promo Nov 7 → Nov 11 10:00 UTC+8 (docs page fetched 2026-11-10), end date "yet to be determined" — the 2026-11-10 snapshot still shows Nov 11 10:00 UTC+8 as the end.
- kie.ai (Nov 8): tokenizer match w/ Qwen, 1M ctx, `lmodel` key, outperforms "all previously released Qwen models" — anecdotal, single tester, unreproducible.
- OrcaRouter (Nov 9): methodical byte-math takedown of the Qwen4-27B reading — 35 GB at Q8 is NOT reproducible from published Qwen3.8-27B weights (~29–31 GB incl. vision tower); the "+6 GB table" also fits wider backbone / more layers / MoE; conclusion: "this is a wish, not a measurement"; no model card, no weights, no API as of 2026-11-09.
- StartupFortune (Nov 8): "No independent benchmark has been published that I could find"; promo is not a pricing strategy; Qwen4 rumour is explicitly only a rumour.
- Stealth Models leak audit (Nov 2): every circulating Qwen4 number is untraceable; Qwen4 NOT released as of 2026-11-10; QwenHF org has zero Qwen4 weights; OpenRouter lists none; Model Studio lists none.
- Qwen official teaser (Nov 6): "The becoming begins" — no model name; Qwen Code v0.26.3/v0.26.5 pre-sizes qwen4 IDs at 1M ctx.

Net: identity, size, architecture, context window, benchmarks — all unverified. No evidence supports a scored report. If Qoder/Alibaba publishes identity + weights/card, re-research then.

